TABLE 3 -- sgimtedepth4dead (#509, 2956c7e) -- the dst_tlb LABEL axis.
Measured 2026-09-09/10 by the Opus 5 seat in scratch clone /tmp/gxopus7g1 (a cp -a of build/).
Baseline NAMED: GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c at HEAD b4d4177 (md5 8479c1eaeb39f006ef0b21cb3b46531a).
build/ was NOT mutated at any point.  Instrument FROZEN once (md5 dcada99957a733e283efbcaf391d4409)
and used for all three detector runs; the reachability control likewise (md5 25ec71f06b58c5c3b43793b7d18a2ee3).

PART 1 -- THE SHIPPED 14-ROW DETECTOR (regress/sgi_mte_fill_probe.py)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    mutant       edit at :1519                                     score   log
    BASE         (none -- the shipped fix)                         14/14   BASE.raw
    M_tlbA       depth == 32  &&  dst_tlb == MTE_TLB_A             14/14   M_tlbA.raw
    M_tlbAB      depth == 32  &&  dst_tlb != MTE_TLB_C             14/14   M_tlbAB.raw

BOTH ARE TOTAL ESCAPES, and stronger than the score says: `diff' against BASE.raw is EMPTY
except the label on line 1.  Every row reported the identical `got' value.  That is what a
detector blind BY CONSTRUCTION looks like -- not a near miss.

Binaries differ, so the edits reached the measurement:
    BASE     e113ca7193a91b8953c4c10f37417ab2   (reproduced bit-for-bit after restore)
    M_tlbA   f43671a0405bb821679f31330a713d31
    M_tlbAB  0d28610d4ba6e72e357b7ad79e907a56

PART 2 -- THE REACHABILITY CONTROL (tlb_reach_control.py; NOT a proposed row set)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Same tiled 32-bit FILL, bg = 0x11223344, driven at each of the three case labels in turn.
Oracle dest[0]:  0x11 = RGBA arm (the #509 repair fired)   0x44 = CI arm (the #509 defect)
Guest-only: an `sd' to CRIME_RE_TLB_A/B/C (0xb5001000/1200/1400) then the MTE registers, on
an unmodified in-tree `-E sgi -e ip32'.  Rung 3.

    binary       MTE_TLB_A   MTE_TLB_B   MTE_TLB_C   log
    BASE         RGBA        RGBA        RGBA        reach_BASE.raw
    M_tlbA       RGBA        CI          CI          reach_M_tlbA.raw
    M_tlbAB      RGBA        RGBA        CI          reach_M_tlbAB.raw

TWO THINGS FOLLOW, and they are different claims:
  * THE SHIPPED FIX IS CORRECT AT ALL THREE LABELS.  BASE is RGBA everywhere.  Nothing here
    is a defect in #509's product code.
  * THE B AND C CELLS ARE REACHABLE AND THE DEFECT IS LIVE IN THEM under M_tlbA -- dest[0]
    returns to 0x44, i.e. the CI PUT assigns buf[0] alone while memory_rw copies four, which
    is the exact leak #509 closed.  The control SEPARATES all three binaries; the shipped
    detector separates none of them.

PART 3 -- WHAT WAS ALREADY DISCLOSED, AND WHAT IS NEW
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRETABLE.out section 1 PREDICTED this escape before table 1 ran, in its own words:
    "DISCLOSED as coverage debt: a mutant conditioning the repair on `dst_tlb == MTE_TLB_A'
     escapes this detector."
So the escape is not a surprise and the round is not accused of missing it.  What is new is
(i) it is now MEASURED rather than predicted, and (ii) the REACHABILITY of the exempted cells
is measured -- which is the fact the floor rule keys on and which no artifact held before.

