kill in a different handler
594:# `#513` sgirekills: five modelled registers ended the host when read back -- and four adversarial passes, three 
of which found something
665:# #513 sgirekills -- kill table 1   (scratch clone /tmp/gx513, frozen instrument)
797:# `#512` pcc2c040kill: one legal guest byte store ended the host
1351:# `#509` sgimtedepth4dead: a bit-count compared against a byte-count, so the branch never ran
1806:# `#505` sgirergbroundtrip: the RGB GET read the pad byte and dropped the red channel — and the panel refuted 
my reason before a different file supplied a better one
2334:# Round #504 sgirandompixel -- a failed pixel read handed the caller `random()` and the destination write stored 
it; the arm now declines with a latched announce, witnessed at rung 3 and backed by a five-mutant table
2507:# Round #503 lunaabsentcpu -- the LUNA-88K interrupt controller called an absent CPU's NULL handler: a store to 
an interrupt mask on the DEFAULT one-CPU machine terminated the simulator; the walk is now bounded to the slots 
DEVINIT connected, with a 37-row rung-3 detector
2606:# Round #502 m88kexcdeliver -- the MC88100 model stopped EVERY guest CPU for seven trap-like exception classes; 
now it delivers them (VBR + 8*vector, shadows and PSR per the manual), and a 22-row detector pins the delivery
3202:# Round #501 pcc2defaultkill -- the `default:` arm of DEVICE_ACCESS(pcc2) ended the host on any access to an 
uncased offset, reads included; now reads keep the served byte and writes are declined, one latched announce per offset
