9837:## Round 480 (#480) -- the detector could not see its own call
9993:### `#479` pass 2 -- the receipt, and four record corrections
10022:## Round 479 (#479) -- a new command did not reset what the old one left
10140:### A live defect `#478` left, found by two seats independently
10152:### And `#478`'s announce could silence itself
10259:### *** THE FLAG CONJUNCT IS LOAD-BEARING, AND `#477`'s COMMENT SAID IT WAS NOT ***
10349:## Round 478 (#478) -- an empty ring was read as a full sector, and 512 stale bytes went to the disk image
10569:## Round 477 (#477) -- a guest data-port WRITE could free the ATAPI transfer the device was still delivering
10747:## Round 476 (#476) -- #475's clamp WOKE a NULL dereference, and two guest accesses killed the host
10908:## Round 475 (#475) -- the ATAPI byte counter stepped past zero, and the transfer length is a guest-chosen byte
11178:## Round 474 (#474) -- a guest READ of the footbridge timer-clear register performed the clear
11273:## Round 473 (#473) -- the ATAPI DATAIN chunking pushed a whole transfer into a ring that cannot hold it, and then reported zero bytes left
11403:## Round 472 (#472) -- an unaligned overlay read took its bytes from the wrong layer
11535:## Round 467 (#467) -- the pty deadline now means SILENCE, not elapsed time
11622:## Round 465 (#465) -- dev_dreamcast_gdrom.c: `data` and `data_len` were released apart
11733:## Round 464 (#464) -- dev_wdc.c: six unlatched `fatal()`, each guest-drivable without bound
11885:## Round 463 (#463) -- dev_dreamcast_asic.c: one guest load ended the host process
12524:## Round 462 (#462) -- one guest store ended the host, and the obvious fix would have left `+0x18` busy forever
13190:## Round 461 (#461) -- both `default:` arms, and roughly 248 of 256 offsets were lethal
13502:## Round 460 (#460) -- one register with no legal first touch
