1: #!/usr/bin/env python3
2: """pcc2widthkills DETECTOR -- the twelve width-guard blocks in DEVICE_ACCESS(pcc2).
3: 
4: WHAT THE FIX DID.  Twelve `if (len != 1)' blocks -- TEN `fatal(); exit(1)' kills that ended the host on
5: a guest-chosen access width, and two #119 warn-once latches that refused it with a
6: process-global static.  The
7: tree's own header says PCC2 registers "can be accessed as bytes, two-bytes, or
8: four-bytes", so the width is LEGAL.  The fix is a DIRECTION SPLIT:
9: 
10:     READS   ACCEPT -- the memcpy above the switch already served them, raw bytes in
11:             address order, width-correct by construction.  The guard discarded a
12:             correct answer.
13:     WRITES  DECLINE + per-instance latched announce -- every STORING write arm uses `idata'
14:             (SCCERR stores a constant 0; PSCALEADJ and IPL store nothing and print),
15:             the big-endian-composed value, which is "the addressed byte" ONLY at
16:             len==1.  Deleting the guard would store the NEIGHBOUR's lane.
17: 
18: CONTRACT (vacuity-floor clause (e)) -- what this detector is designed to catch:
19: 
20:   CATCHES
21:     * reinstatement of the kill at any of the SIX GUEST-reachable blocks (survival
22:       rows paired with a liveness observable, because exit status cannot tell
23:       "declined and quit" from "died with status 0");
24:     * *** pass 2: the two FOLDED-IN arms, IPL and MASK, had NO ROW -- twelve blocks
25:       converted, ten given rows, and the shipped contract did not say so.  A seat
26:       found it by sibling parity: MASK is GENCTL's twin and had none of GENCTL's rows.
27:       Repaired: IPL is EVEN and therefore the SIXTH guest-reachable block (survival +
28:       message rows); MASK is odd (operator rows) and gets GENCTL's readback. ***
29:     * reinstatement at any of the six OPERATOR-only blocks (VECBASE, PSCALEADJ, SCCICR,
30:       SCCRX, SCSIICR, MASK; the T1CTL/T1ICR labels are odd too but share TxCTL/TxICR's
31:       blocks), through the debugger's `put h' at an odd address -- MEASURED to warn
32:       and store and kill
33:       (artifacts/pcc2widthkills/operator_reach_20260903.out);
34:     * *** DELETE instead of decline on the write side -- the lane hazard.  `st.h
35:       0xAABB' to GENCTL must leave GENCTL unchanged; a bare deletion stores 0xBB,
36:       VECBASE's lane, because (uint8_t) idata is the HIGHEST-address byte ***;
37:     * an accidental per-lane compose (GENCTL would read 0xAA);
38:     * the value a wide READ composes -- lane order and width -- not merely survival;
39:     * loss of the latch in either direction: dropped `|=' floods (same site twice
40:       must announce ONCE), and one bit shared across blocks silences (two sites must
41:       announce TWICE);
42:     * the de-escalation clause: at the five even blocks with `acc' rows a legal byte write
43:       lands and reads back through the arm's own mask with NO decline message; at all
44:       twelve, `acc all' pins NO decline and survival (a guard grown to refuse bytes); at
45:       the two print-only arms the body's own print is the proof (`acc pscale ign',
46:       `acc ipl ro').  SCCERR's byte side is value-identical (always 0) and is disclosed,
47:       not claimed.
48: 
49:   THE ENUMERATION (pass 3 class closure, pass 4 domain repair).  Twelve blocks x NINE
50:   clause-(d) shapes, the helper's own two operations, and four access widths.  Two
51:   consecutive passes found breaches of ONE class -- a block with no channel for the
52:   ANNOUNCE-THEN-FALL-THROUGH shape (guard kept, announce kept, `break' removed, the
53:   halfword LANDS) -- at MASK, then at four odd arms, then (pass 3, MEASURED 82/82 by a
54:   seat) at VECBASE, whose `rb vecbase' row is GENCTL's neighbour-lane check and never
55:   writes wide to VECBASE's own arm.  So the space is written down, cell by cell.
56:   M = measured kill (log named in CHANGELOG/PRETABLE); S = same channel as a measured
57:   shape at that arm (the mutant lands the write exactly as the measured one does);
58:   E = equivalent by construction, with its warrant.  Shapes: DEL guard deleted; LEN
59:   `len != 1' -> `len > 2' (halfword lands, word declined); LEN2 its MIRROR, `len != 1' ->
60:   `len == 2' (halfword declined, WORD lands -- named by the codex seat on pass 3); KILL
61:   verbatim exit(1) reinstated; ALIAS one enum member for two blocks; FALL announce-then-
62:   fall-through; SWAP guard operand `len' -> `idata > 0xff'; GROW the guard widened to
63:   decline the LEGAL byte width too (`len != 1' -> `len != 0'), the de-escalation clause.
64: 
65:       block      DEL   LEN   LEN2  KILL  ALIAS FALL  SWAP  GROW   FALL channel
66:       GENCTL     M     S     W     S     C     M     M     A/C    rb genctl (table 1 M_NOBREAK)
67:       VECBASE    S     S     W     M     C     M     C     C      rb vecbase own  (pass-3 repair)
68:       PSCALEADJ  S     S     W     S     C     M     C     A/C    op pscale noig  (message; acc pscale ign)
69:       TxCTL      S     M     W     S     C     M     C     A/C    rb t2ctl (FALL: part 3b, t2 and t1)
70:       TxICR      M     M     W     S     C     S     C     A/C    rb t2icr
71:       SCCERR     S     M     S     S     C     E     C     A/C    E: the arm stores 0 and nothing in
72:                                                                   the model ever stores a nonzero
73:                                                                   SCCERR (deriver: every writer of
74:                                                                   pcctwo_reg[], grep -F 'pcctwo_reg[';
75:                                                                   the counter memcpy's 8-byte span
76:                                                                   is pcc2counter8, disclosed)
77:       SCCICR     S     S     W     S     C     M     C     C      rb sccicr
78:       SCCTX      M     M     W     S     C     S     C     A/C    rb scctx
79:       SCCRX      S     S     W     S     C     M     C     C      rb sccrx
80:       SCSIICR    S     S     W     S     C     M     C     C      rb scsiicr
81:       IPL        S     S     W     M     C     M     C     A/C    hwr ipl noig    (pass-3 repair; acc ipl ro;
82:                                                                   the write body prints once)
83:       MASK       M     M     W     M     C     M     C     C      rb mask
84:       C  = the cardinality row `latch all' (twelve wide writes, twelve announces): ALIAS,
85:            any collision drops the count; SWAP: the bare swap drops the length test and every byte preset
86:            kills it (part 7, 95/171); a value-test QUALIFIER on the guard is caught only
87:            for the VALUES rows drive AT EVERY ARM -- 3 (`latch all'), 1 (`latch all
88:            one') and 0 (`latch all zero') -- and, per arm, for whatever that arm's own
89:            wide-write rows drive (0xaabb, 0xaab8, 0x0022 ...); any other constant is not
90:            (passes 7-8; Opus F13).
91:       W  = `latch all w' (twelve WORD writes via put w, twelve announces): a `len == 2'
92:            guard at ANY arm lets the word land silently and drops the count.  SCCERR's
93:            own word rows (wrd/wwr sccerr) are its S.
94:       A/C = the arm's own `acc' row, AND `acc all' (twelve legal GUEST byte stores, ZERO
95:            declines): a guard grown to refuse bytes at ANY arm announces and reds it.
96:            Blocks marked C alone have no per-arm acc row; `acc all' is their channel.
97:            NOT the debugger's `put b': it calls memory_rw with NO_EXCEPTIONS, which does not
98:            dispatch to a DM_DEFAULT device, so a `put b' row could not see the grown guard
99:            (MEASURED: 95/96 in part 3 and 96/96 in part 3b, the mutation proven in the binary).  `put h/w/d' go
100:            through the store_Nbit_word helpers and do reach the arms.
101:       DEL/LEN/KILL cells marked S land the write, or die, exactly as the measured shape at
102:       that arm does, and the arm's own dcl / survival
103:       / readback rows are the channel.  KILL cells' channel is the survival PAIR (exit
104:       status plus the liveness observable), which varies under a reinstated kill by
105:       construction; the CHANNEL rule's 'survival-only' names a survival oracle at a
106:       REFUSAL-effect site, which a kill is not.  `d->warned' is a 32-bit field with twelve bits assigned.
