13: #
14: #  *** IT BEGAN AS A 6-ROW WITNESS AND IS NOW A 14-ROW DETECTOR.  The banner that used to stand
15: #  here -- "a witness, not a detector; its rows are expected to FAIL; it must not be gated" --
16: #  was true of the 6-row version against HEAD and is FALSE of this one, which scores 14/14 on the
17: #  fix and 10/14 on a verbatim reinstatement.  The pass-2 codex seat caught the staleness. ***
18: #
19: #  It is STILL NOT WIRED INTO A GATE, and that is a separate decision from what it is.
20: #
21: #  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
22: #  THE ORACLE IS `dest[0]' OF A TILED **FILL**, AND EVERY OTHER CHANNEL I PROPOSED WAS REFUSED.
23: #  From the grok design review, each point measured against the source rather than argued:
24: #
25: #  * A PRE-PAINTED TAIL CANNOT WORK.  CI PUT does not replicate buf[0] across the span and does not
26: #    leave a tail: it writes buf[0] at the lowest address and buf[1..bufdepth-1] as uninitialised
27: #    stack, and memory_rw memcpys `bufdepth' bytes.  So the paint is OVERWRITTEN WITH GARBAGE.  A row
28: #    asserting "tail still painted" reds on HEAD because the path RAN -- which reads as "the witness
29: #    never reached MTE".  A row asserting "tail != paint" is true on HEAD *and* after the fix.
30: #
31: #  * COPY CANNOT WITNESS THIS AT ALL.  Source `aa bb cc dd': CI GET takes buf[0] == 0xaa and CI PUT
32: #    writes 0xaa at dest[0]; RGBA GET reconstructs 0xaabbccdd and RGBA PUT also writes 0xaa there.
33: #    The first byte of a copy is the one byte CI already gets right, and the broken bytes are exactly
34: #    the uninitialised ones that must not be read.  "If the witness is a blit, refuse it."
35: #
36: #  * FILL IS DETERMINISTIC BECAUSE IT NEVER GETs.  With bg = 0x11223344:
37: #        CI   PUT -> buf[0] = (uint8_t)bg          -> dest[0] = 0x44   (the LOW byte)
38: #        RGBA PUT -> [bg>>24, bg>>16, bg>>8, bg]   -> dest[0] = 0x11   (the HIGH byte)
39: #    dest[1..3] are uninitialised on HEAD.  **DO NOT ASSERT THEM THERE.**
40: #
41: #  *** THAT SENTENCE USED TO END "only the top byte of the big-endian word is READ", WHICH IS
42: #  FALSE AND WAS CAUGHT BY THE PASS-1 CODEX SEAT.  The probe executes `lw' and masks afterwards:
43: #  it READS four bytes and ASSERTS one.  Corrected 2026-09-07 -- the distinction matters because
