The numeric-tag premise needs qualification: some entries are harness rounds, and `pcc2widthkills` uses a row-name comment rather than a numbered tag. I mapped those to the product edit they defend.

The matching `gdromexitsix/killtable*` directories concern **#489**. Its co-located #490 follow-up was also checked: format decline at `dev_dreamcast_gdrom.c:790` and command decline at :915 belong respectively to `case 0x30` and `default` of switch :683. Neither is multi-label.

For Q2, the actual dataflow is:

| Multi-label edit | Selector dependence within the enclosing function | Classification |
|---|---|---|
| PCC2 TxCTL | `relative_addr` selects `d->pcctwo_reg[relative_addr]`, read and written at :559–560 and :563. | **FLOOR** |
| PCC2 TxICR | Same indexed lvalue at :579–580/:600. The body also re-tests `relative_addr` at :582/:585/:589/:594 to select pending-timer effects. | **FLOOR** |
| SGI #509 | `dst_tlb` contributes to **`dst_mode` at :1499**. The guarded compound assignment reads and writes that lvalue at :1521. | **FLOOR** |
| WDC #485 security block | Labels are `WDCC_SEC_SET_PASSWORD`, `WDCC_SEC_UNLOCK`, `WDCC_SEC_ERASE_PREPARE`, `WDCC_SEC_ERASE_UNIT`, `WDCC_SEC_FREEZE_LOCK`, `WDCC_SEC_DISABLE_PASSWORD`. The selector supplies neither `d->error`’s incoming value nor the constant assignment to `d->int_assert`; there is no selector re-test in the block. | **(e)** for this label-axis census; the repair is unconditional. |
| M88K #502 tail | Labels are `M88K_EXCEPTION_` prefixed **MISALIGNED_ACCESS, UNIMPLEMENTED_OPCODE, PRIVILEGE_VIOLATION, BOUNDS_CHECK_VIOLATION, ILLEGAL_INTEGER_DIVIDE, INTEGER_OVERFLOW, ERROR**. Although `vector` contributes to `cpu->pc` at :863, the edited shared body at :961 contains only `break`: no lvalue access or selector re-test. | **(e) / no edited guard** under the stated criterion. |

PCC2’s CHIPID/CHIPREV and counter/compare groups are genuine shared blocks, but **they are not edits defended by `pcc2widthkills`**. Footbridge’s folded timer addresses likewise do not become additional case labels.

For Q3:

| FLOOR site | Labels actually driven by the shipped detector | Labels with no row |
|---|---|---|
| PCC2 TxCTL | **T1CTL and T2CTL.** [pcc2_width_probe.py:427](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/pcc2_width_probe.py:427) defines their distinct offsets. The T2 readback loop is at :674; T1’s own readback loop at :1328; T1 wider-write rows at :1215. | **None** |
| PCC2 TxICR | **T1ICR and T2ICR**, through those same explicit per-label loops. The joint pending-timer session also exercises both labels at :1153 onward. | **None** |
| SGI #509 | **MTE_TLB_A only.** [sgi_mte_fill_probe.py:219](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sgi_mte_fill_probe.py:219) programs fill modes from the depth constants; :251 programs the copy mode. All leave the destination-selector field zero, which the header maps to A. | **MTE_TLB_B, MTE_TLB_C** |

Applying the existing depth cells gives **{B, C} × {8, 16, 32, 64}: eight missing label/depth cells**. This does not require replicating every detector assertion or adding a COPY cross-product.

Two packet premises need tightening:

- The detector has **14 scored assertions**, but `live`, `devsig`, and `paint ok` do not dispatch MTE. **Every transfer-producing session selects A** is the accurate statement.
- “Only DEPTH flows from `mode` into the repair operands” is too broad. The source and destination buffer fields also flow through `src_tlb`/`dst_tlb` into `src_mode`/`dst_mode` at :1498–1499. **COPY specifically does not**; its later test at :1529 leaves its classification **(e)** intact.

For Q4, **#509 is the sole positive candidate**. I would measure the missing **B-label, depth-32 counterpart of `fill top`** first, against the **already documented `M_tlbA`**. Its exact edit is the packet’s qualification of the :1519 comparison by `&& dst_tlb == MTE_TLB_A`. The row should assert the existing correct RGBA first-byte result at B. This addresses the recorded information-exposure defect using the existing defined-byte oracle. There is no newly discovered candidate to rank ahead of it.

